## License Scope

This MIT License covers the software components of the Costa Rica Tree Atlas:
all TypeScript, JavaScript, configuration, build scripts, and tests in this
repository.

**Content and data are licensed separately:**

- Editorial content, species descriptions, comparison guides, and glossary
  entries are licensed under **CC BY 4.0** — see
  [LICENSE-CONTENT.md](LICENSE-CONTENT.md).

- The species dataset (Darwin Core Archive) is licensed under **CC BY 4.0** —
  see [LICENSE-DATA.md](LICENSE-DATA.md).

- Indigenous knowledge content (traditional names, ceremonial uses, oral
  histories, and any material attributed to indigenous communities) is
  governed by [docs/INDIGENOUS_KNOWLEDGE_GOVERNANCE.md](docs/INDIGENOUS_KNOWLEDGE_GOVERNANCE.md)
  and is NOT covered by the CC BY 4.0 grant. Reuse requires the consent
  process documented in that policy, regardless of the license that
  applies to the surrounding code or content.

- Third-party assets (photographs, illustrations, audio recordings) carry
  their own attribution and license terms, which are visible on each page
  and embedded in image metadata. Most photographs are sourced from
  iNaturalist under Creative Commons licenses (typically CC BY-NC); see
  per-image credit lines.

When in doubt about reuse of a specific element, open an issue and ask. The
project's goal is to be cited, taught from, and built upon — but not at the
expense of indigenous self-determination or photographer attribution.
